Nethack is vastly more complicated an more polished than Moria. Moria, on the
other hand, is more "role-playing" oriented, in that you prepare for an 
adventure in a village, where you return to recuperate, sell loot etc.
One of the major flaws in Moria (at least the version I played a while back)
is that the dungeon level is not saved when you leave it -- you can't come
back to an interesting place, once you've gone down or up. In NH, on the 
other hand, you get to know the dungeon very well, if you manage to do a 
good game. There is more variety (as in monsters, abilities, items) in NH, 
as well as a nicely-constructed "plot". On most machines the graphics are
better, too: I got serious eyestrain from Moria (whereas NH just causes loss
of sleep and social contacts, not to mention flunking courses...).

IMHO, Moria (and Angband) are pretty weak compared to NH, although they do
have some nice features.

